-- title:
--   Igusa nodes over supersingular places under level transport, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ equal to $3$, an $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, $\kappa$ its residue field, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC` over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set). Write $\bar F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H=\ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times)$, and assume the base-changed level-$M'$ field sits inside it via `hle`. The data are: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from the base-changed level-$M'$ field onto its $\kappa$-model, with residue given coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; valuation subrings $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda\subset\bar F$ indexed by $\lambda\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s\subset\bar F$ indexed by $s\in W$. The hypotheses on these, summarised here, are: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ consists of the $f$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $fy=x$; each $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction mod $q$ sends $[1:0]$ to $\lambda$; $\lambda\mapsto O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ is injective and this family is permuted by pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, is fixed by all such pullbacks, and contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ for all $a\in A$; and, for $f$ in the integers of $R_0$ that is regular at every place where the base-changed $j$ is regular and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ and $f-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ whenever the residue of $a\in A$ is the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$. Further, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ onto the $\kappa$-Igusa field `xHFunctionFieldC` of level $q^2M'$ and $H$, with integers $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$, the integers of $R_0$ being exactly the functions mapping into $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$; $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is a finite set of places of that $\kappa$-Igusa field with $|N^{\mathrm{Ig}}|=|W|$, and there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from the $\kappa$-level-$M'$ field to it compatible with the residue maps of $R_0$ and $R$ such that $Q\in N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ iff $Q$ is the $j$-pullback-characterised place of some $s\in W$; finally $g_\lambda$ is, for each $\lambda$, an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $\bar F$ lying in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` ($\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) and equal to `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ sending $[1:0]$ to $\lambda$ mod $q$. The conclusion asserts a family of places $x_{\lambda,s}$ of the $\kappa$-Igusa field, for $\lambda\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $s\in W$, all lying in $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, such that for each $\lambda$ there is a ring homomorphism $j_\lambda$ from the $\kappa$-level-$M'$ field to the $\kappa$-Igusa field which is the identity on $\kappa$, satisfies $R.\mathrm{residue}(g_\lambda f)=j_\lambda(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ for all $f$ in the integers of $R_0$, pulls back the valuation subring of $x_{\lambda,s}$ to that of $s$ for every $s\in W$, and again characterises $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ as the set of places $Q$ for which some $s\in W$ has $g'\in O_s\iff j_\lambda g'\in O_Q$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case, at the rigid auxiliary level imposed by the prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the statement that the supersingular places of $X_0(M')_\kappa$ transport, along each level automorphism moving $[1:0]$ to a given point of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, to nodes on the Igusa component indexed by that point, with a $\kappa$-linear reduction homomorphism realising the transport. It feeds the construction of the charted semistable covering of the full-level modular curve in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
